	                transport error.

   EXAMPLES
	#include <proto/exec.h>
	#include <proto/dos.h>
	#include <proto/mailbox.h>

	APTR MailboxBase = OpenResource("mailbox.resource");
	if (MailboxBase)
	{
	    ULONG state = MB_SetGPIOState(42, 1);                /* 42 = status LED */
	    Printf("Status LED set to: %ld\n", state);
	}

   NOTE
	As of V1.1 the call gives up after three seconds without an answer from
	the firmware and returns -1. Prior to V1.1 it had no time limit and no
	way to report a failure: a mailbox that did not answer stopped the task
	for good.

   SEE ALSO
	mailbox.resource/MB_GetGPIOState()

mailbox.resource/MB_SetPowerState           mailbox.resource/MB_SetPowerState

   NAME
	MB_SetPowerState -- power a device domain on or off

   SYNOPSIS
	state = MB_SetPowerState( id, state )
	d0                        d0  d1

	ULONG MB_SetPowerState(ULONG, ULONG);

   FUNCTION
	Powers a VideoCore-managed device domain on or off, using
	property tag SET_POWER_STATE (0x00028001).

   INPUTS
	id              The device to set, by the firmware's id: 0 SD card,
	                3 USB host controller.
	state           Bit 0: 1 to power on, 0 to power off.

   RESULTS
	state           The state actually applied, or -1 on a mailbox
	                transport error.

   EXAMPLES
	#include <proto/exec.h>
	#include <proto/dos.h>
	#include <proto/mailbox.h>

	APTR MailboxBase = OpenResource("mailbox.resource");
	if (MailboxBase)
	{
	    ULONG state = MB_SetPowerState(3, 1);                /* 3 = USB host controller */
	    Printf("USB power set to: %ld\n", state);
	}

   NOTE
	As of V1.1 the call gives up after three seconds without an answer from
	the firmware and returns -1. Prior to V1.1 it had no time limit and no
	way to report a failure: a mailbox that did not answer stopped the task
	for good.

   SEE ALSO
	mailbox.resource/MB_GetPowerState()

mailbox.resource/MB_StringCommand           mailbox.resource/MB_StringCommand

   NAME
	MB_StringCommand -- send a vcgencmd-style text command

   SYNOPSIS
	length = MB_StringCommand( command, reply, reply_capacity )
	d0                         a0       a1     d0

	ULONG MB_StringCommand(STRPTR, STRPTR, ULONG);

   FUNCTION
	Sends a null-terminated ASCII command string using the
	GET_GENCMD_RESULT property tag (0x00030080), the same tag
	vcgencmd uses on Linux, and copies the firmware's text reply
	into the caller's buffer.

   INPUTS
	command         A null-terminated ASCII command string, e.g.
	                "measure_temp". May not exceed 1023 characters.
	reply           A buffer to receive the reply text, or NULL to discard
	                it.
	reply_capacity  The size in bytes of the reply buffer. The reply is
	                truncated to whichever is smaller: this value or 1024.

   RESULTS
	length          The reply length reported by the firmware, or -1 on a
	                mailbox transport error or an oversized command
	                string.

   EXAMPLES
	#include <proto/exec.h>
	#include <proto/dos.h>
	#include <proto/mailbox.h>

	APTR MailboxBase = OpenResource("mailbox.resource");
	if (MailboxBase)
	{
	    UBYTE reply[256];

	    MB_StringCommand("measure_temp", reply, sizeof(reply));
	    Printf("vcgencmd reply: %s\n", reply);
	}

   NOTE
	As of V1.1 the call gives up after three seconds without an answer from
	the firmware and returns -1. Prior to V1.1 it had no time limit and no
	way to report a failure: a mailbox that did not answer stopped the task
	for good.

   SEE ALSO
	mailbox.resource/MB_RawCommand()

